1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
Three nights in a hospital bed.

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,200
Then three weeks of rehab.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,940
And Medicare's share of the rehab bill…

4
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:08,220
is zero.

5
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,220
Six thousand three hundred dollars comes

6
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:12,940
out of your savings instead.

7
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:15,800
Because of one word written on your chart.

8
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,240
The word is observation.

9
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:22,380
By the end of this, you will know what

10
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:25,040
that word means, the three-day rule it

11
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,780
quietly breaks, and the one question that

12
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:30,020
keeps six thousand dollars in your account.

13
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:33,280
That question has to be asked on day one.

14
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,600
Not at checkout.

15
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,000
This is educational, not medical, financial

16
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:39,120
or legal advice.

17
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:42,080
It's the fine print, read out loud.

18
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:44,540
First, the word.

19
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:47,540
You can lie in a hospital bed for three

20
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,780
nights, with a wristband, a nurse, a tray,

21
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:51,960
a bill.

22
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:54,300
And on paper, never be admitted.

23
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,140
Observation means the hospital is watching

24
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,220
you as an outpatient.

25
00:00:59,020 --> 00:00:59,820
Same bed.

26
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:01,280
Different column in the ledger.

27
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:04,480
Here is how Medicare draws the line, for

28
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:05,380
twenty twenty-six.

29
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:08,100
If your doctor expects you to need at least

30
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:10,380
two midnights in the hospital, you are

31
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:12,300
generally admitted as an inpatient.

32
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,280
If the expectation is less than two midnights,

33
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:16,540
you are observed.

34
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:19,520
It's called the two-midnight rule, and

35
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,340
it has been on the books since twenty thirteen.

36
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:24,720
Since twenty twenty-four, Medicare Advantage

37
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,300
plans have to follow it too.

38
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:28,960
The scale of this is not small.

39
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:31,580
The last time the inspector general counted,

40
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:33,920
in twenty twelve, there were about one

41
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,180
and a half million observation stays in

42
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:37,060
a single year.

43
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:39,600
So here is how you check yours.

44
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,100
There is a form.

45
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:44,200
It's called the Medicare Outpatient Observation

46
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,000
Notice.

47
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,060
If you've been under observation for more

48
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:49,400
than twenty-four hours, the hospital must

49
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,500
hand it to you within thirty-six hours

50
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,100
of when the observation started.

51
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,700
It says, in writing, that you are an outpatient.

52
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:00,000
If nobody has handed you that form, ask.

53
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:02,280
The question is seven words.

54
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:05,280
Am I an inpatient, or under observation?

55
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:09,200
Second, the rule the word breaks.

56
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:12,320
Medicare pays for rehab in a skilled nursing

57
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:15,300
facility only after a qualifying hospital

58
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,100
stay.

59
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,180
The stay has to be at least three days

60
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,720
in a row as an inpatient.

61
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:22,260
The count starts the day you are admitted.

62
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,680
The day you leave does not count.

63
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,900
And the nights you spent under observation,

64
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:29,420
or in the emergency room, do not count.

65
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,160
Even if you slept there.

66
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:32,780
Now run the number.

67
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,100
Two people.

68
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:37,120
Same fall, same hospital, same three nights,

69
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,540
same twenty days of rehab afterward.

70
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,360
The first was admitted.

71
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:43,600
Days one through twenty in the facility,

72
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:44,820
Medicare pays.

73
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:47,600
Her cost for those twenty days: zero.

74
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:49,980
The second was under observation.

75
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,360
No qualifying stay, so Medicare pays nothing

76
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,340
toward the facility.

77
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,020
The twenty twenty-five national median

78
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:59,340
for a semi-private room in a nursing home,

79
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,620
from the CareScout Cost of Care survey,

80
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:03,160
is about three hundred fifteen dollars

81
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,240
a day.

82
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,130
Twenty days… six thousand three hundred

83
00:03:07,130 --> 00:03:07,930
dollars.

84
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,440
A private room, about three hundred fifty-five

85
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,040
a day: seven thousand one hundred.

86
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:16,140
Make it thirty days, which is common after

87
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:16,940
a hip.

88
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:19,300
The admitted patient pays the twenty twenty-six

89
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,560
rate of two hundred seventeen dollars a

90
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:23,550
day for days twenty-one through thirty:

91
00:03:23,550 --> 00:03:25,420
two thousand one hundred seventy.

92
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,810
The observed patient: nine thousand four

93
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:29,610
hundred fifty.

94
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:32,580
And a Medicare supplement does not rescue

95
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:33,380
you here.

96
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:35,940
A Medigap policy pays its share of bills

97
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:36,940
Medicare approves.

98
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:39,840
If Medicare approves nothing, the supplement

99
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,640
pays nothing.

100
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,740
Put that against a nest egg.

101
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:45,580
Three hundred thousand dollars, drawn at

102
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:48,100
four percent, is a thousand dollars a month.

103
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:51,060
Six thousand three hundred dollars is six

104
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,720
months of your own paycheck, gone in three

105
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:55,560
weeks, because of a word.

106
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:59,120
How to check yours: it's the same question,

107
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,200
asked early.

108
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,520
If the doctor says you'll likely be here

109
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,780
two nights or more, ask whether you've

110
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:05,580
been admitted.

111
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:11,160
Third, the paperwork that decides it, before

112
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,020
and after.

113
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:13,880
Before.

114
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:16,020
If you're on a Medicare Advantage plan,

115
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,800
open the Evidence of Coverage.

116
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:20,300
It's the thick booklet, and it's online

117
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,280
in your plan account.

118
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:24,180
Find the section on skilled nursing facility

119
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:24,980
care.

120
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:27,100
There is a line that says whether a prior

121
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,560
hospital stay is required.

122
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,260
Some plans waive the three-day rule.

123
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:32,460
Some don't.

124
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,920
You are allowed to change plans until December

125
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:37,360
seventh, and that one line is a reason

126
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,680
to read it before then.

127
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,440
Plans can also charge a daily copay in

128
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,660
the first twenty days, so read the line

129
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:44,520
below it too.

130
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:46,420
After.

131
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:48,480
If you were admitted and then the hospital

132
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:51,020
switched you to observation, since twenty

133
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:53,140
twenty-five you can appeal that switch

134
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:54,500
while you are still in the bed.

135
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:56,880
They hand you a change-of-status notice,

136
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,760
and an independent reviewer decides, usually

137
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,560
within a day.

138
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,980
But if you were never admitted in the first

139
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,840
place, there is nothing to appeal.

140
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,660
Which is why the question belongs on day

141
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:08,460
one.

142
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,960
So three questions, in order.

143
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,780
Am I an inpatient, or under observation?

144
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,720
Can I have that in writing?

145
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,460
And, if rehab is coming: do I have three

146
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,600
inpatient days yet?

147
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,700
One word on a chart moves thousands of

148
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,960
dollars from Medicare's column to yours.

149
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:30,520
The same bed, the same nights, the same

150
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,320
tray.

151
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:33,580
The only thing that changed was the paperwork,

152
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:36,580
and the paperwork is the part you can check.

153
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,820
One thing to do this week.

154
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,700
If you're on an Advantage plan, find the

155
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:43,540
skilled nursing line in your Evidence of

156
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:45,620
Coverage, and decide whether it changes

157
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:47,120
your December seventh decision.

158
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,000
If you're on Original Medicare, write the

159
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,380
seven-word question on a card and put it

160
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:53,380
with your Medicare card.

161
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:55,580
Your State Health Insurance Assistance

162
00:05:55,580 --> 00:05:57,980
Program is free, and a counselor there

163
00:05:57,980 --> 00:05:59,920
can walk through your own plan with you.

164
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:02,660
A fee-only fiduciary can run what a bill

165
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,120
like this does to your plan.

166
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:07,000
New numbers every Tuesday and Friday.

167
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,840
Subscribe, so the next one finds you.

168
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,200
Will your money last as long as you do?
